menu "XPRS firmware updates"

config XPRS_OTA_PULL
    bool "Let the station fetch its own image over HTTP"
    default y
    help
        With this on, the station can be told a channel or a URL and will
        go and get the image itself (cmd:update with no bytes attached).
        That convenience costs static RAM: esp_http_client and the TLS
        stack it drags in are linked in permanently, whether an update is
        running or not.

        Measured on the T-Dongle-S3, which lives at roughly 13 KB free
        with the radios up, that cost is enough to leave the HTTP server
        unable to start at boot. Turn this off on such a board: the push
        door (POST /api/update, and the mesh lane behind it) still works,
        so the image is carried to the station instead of fetched by it.
        docs/device.md section 6 states the rule and the number.

endmenu
